[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2650550831","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102699#issuecomment-2650550831","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102699","id":2650550831,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6d_DIv","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-11T11:36:35Z","updated_at":"2025-02-11T11:36:35Z","body":"Is it an issue? Seems like a reasonable way to handle it. C/C++ do the same with `'` separator:\n```c++\nint a1 = 0x'1A; // not valid\nint a2 = 0x1'A; // valid\nint b1 = 0b'11; // not valid\nint b2 = 0b1'1; // valid\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2650550831/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2650555086","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102699#issuecomment-2650555086","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102699","id":2650555086,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6d_ELO","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-11T11:38:43Z","updated_at":"2025-02-11T11:38:43Z","body":"The [GDScript Literal documentation](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_basics.html#literals) says that:\n> Integers and floats can have their numbers separated with `_` to make them more readable.\n\nWhich implies this limitation, but could be a little more explicit if desired","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2650555086/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2651073173","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102699#issuecomment-2651073173","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102699","id":2651073173,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6eBCqV","user":{"login":"Mangochicken13","id":97166753,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcqloQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97166753?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mangochicken13","html_url":"https://github.com/Mangochicken13","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mangochicken13/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mangochicken13/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mangochicken13/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mangochicken13/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mangochicken13/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mangochicken13/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mangochicken13/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mangochicken13/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mangochicken13/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-11T14:58:44Z","updated_at":"2025-02-11T14:58:44Z","body":"> Is it an issue? Seems like a reasonable way to handle it. C/C++ do the same with `'` separator:\n> ```c++\n> int a1 = 0x'1A; // not valid\n> int a2 = 0x1'A; // valid\n> int b1 = 0b'11; // not valid\n> int b2 = 0b1'1; // valid\n> ```\n\nI mean, it's in no way a deal-breaking, or even major issue, more just something that I thought was possible, tried, and was surprised when it wasn't. Especially as it's a change from being previously possible (in 4.1-beta2 and, as far as I know, back to at least 4.0)\n\nThe other thing that throws me off about this specifically is that in GDScript the number (eg `0x_1F`) is still seemingly read as a number, at least as far as the syntax highlighter is concerned, which differs from the C++ example where the `1A` in `0x'1A` isn't highlighted since it isn't read as a number\n\nIf this change doesn't fit in GDScript or the current implementation is deemed better I won't be losing sleep over it though","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2651073173/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2651370640","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102699#issuecomment-2651370640","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102699","id":2651370640,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6eCLSQ","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-11T16:37:46Z","updated_at":"2025-02-11T16:37:46Z","body":"This is highly debatable, but I see the following arguments in favor of the current behavior:\n\n1. In my opinion, it makes sense not to support this for binary and hexadecimal literals, since it is not supported for decimal ones. `_0001` is an identifier, not a literal, so the `0b` and `0x` prefixes impose the same restrictions on the digit group after them.\n2. Not that we thought much about this, but it was dictated by the tokenizer code that parses different types and digit groups of numeric literals. For the same reason, you can't write `1._23` or `1e_23`.\n3. Also, the very name \"separator\" implies that it can only appear **between** digits. On the other hand, trailing underscores are allowed. If I remember correctly, I wanted to remove it, but I left it only because this case was in tests.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2651370640/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]